# BS 8414 surrogate project — git ignores
#
# Written once and copied into every surrogate project (see APPS.md). What is
# kept out is what training regenerates: weights, extracted arrays, rendered
# figures, and the venv. What is kept IN is everything that records a decision —
# source, configs, run logs, results notes, and the shipped app asset table.
#
# Nothing here deletes anything; git only stops tracking these paths.

# ── environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each project has its own venv and they are never shared. Torch + CUDA wheels
# are several GB and are reinstalled from requirements.txt, not from git.
venv/
.venv/
env/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# ── python bytecode / tooling caches ──────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── model checkpoints ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The weights themselves, wherever they sit: 3 MB (thermocouple member) to
# 34 MB (FunDiff DiT) each, across hundreds of models*/ run directories. A
# checkpoint is reproducible from its seed + config.
#
# Ignored BY EXTENSION, not by directory, and that is deliberate: git cannot
# re-include a file inside an excluded directory, so a `models_*/` rule would
# also bury evaluation_part1.json, metrics.json, run_summary.json and
# history_member*.json — the small files that carry the score and the training
# curve for every run. Those are the provenance of every number in
# PART1_RESULTS.md, so they stay tracked while the weights beside them do not.
#
# By extension, the `model/` package and `model*.py` modules (model.py,
# model_part1.py, model/fae.py, model/dit.py) are untouched source.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx

# ── extracted / cached arrays ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# data/part1_slices alone is ~1.01 GB (185 cases). Regenerate with
# extract_slices_part1.py (~50 min, restartable), never from git.
data/
*.npz
*.npy
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl
*.pickle

# ── generated outputs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rendered by evaluate/validate/plot scripts from the checkpoints above.
outputs/
outputs_*/
figures/
fields/
*.mp4
*.gif

# ── keep: the ONE deployment model each Streamlit app serves ──────────────
# Chosen and justified by ..\select_best_model.py, which also writes the
# matching app_assets/selected_model.json. These are the only weights a fresh
# clone needs to make a prediction; every other run above stays ignored.
# A path that does not exist in a given project is simply inert, which is what
# keeps this file byte-identical across all of them.
#   KAN          models_part1_r4_seed48    combined valid+test TC R2 0.8526
#   MLP          models_part1_bal_s61_r2   combined valid+test TC R2 0.8096
#   FunDiff      models_part1_fundiff_r1   test DiT(gen) R2 0.8658
#   FunDiff-KAN  models_part1_fundiff_r1   test DiT(gen) R2 0.8740
# 139.5 MB in total (KAN 9.8, MLP 9.8, FunDiff 58.6, FunDiff-KAN 61.3), largest
# single file 32.5 MB. Every file is under GitHub's 50 MB warning and its 100 MB
# hard limit, but the repo grows by ~140 MB per selection change, so use git-lfs
# if the destination repo will see several.
!models_part1_r4_seed48/part1_member*.pt
!models_part1_bal_s61_r2/part1_member*.pt
!models_part1_fundiff_r1/fae_best.pt
!models_part1_fundiff_r1/dit_best.pt

# ── keep: the shipped Streamlit asset table ───────────────────────────────
# Small, exact, and required to run the app on a machine without the FDS
# corpus. Re-exported by ..\export_app_assets.py. Stated explicitly so both
# survive if a broader data/asset rule is ever added above.
!app_assets/
!app_assets/part1_materials.json
!app_assets/selected_model.json

# ── run logs: TRACKED on purpose ──────────────────────────────────────────
# ~7.6 MB of plain text across all projects, and it is the experimental record —
# PART1_RESULTS.md and VARIANCE_RECORD.md quote per-member best-valid-loss and
# stop-epoch numbers straight out of these files, and runs are versioned as
# paired .log/.err.log rather than as git branches. Losing them loses the
# provenance of every reported number.
# Uncomment the two lines below if a repo ever needs them out.
# *.log
# *.err.log

# ── editors / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ── agent working notes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md is the working brief for this repo's own agent sessions: internal
# conventions, non-negotiables and in-progress reasoning. It is not part of the
# published artefact and is deliberately untracked. README.md carries everything
# a reader of the repository needs.
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# ── secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.key
*.pem
